					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-159209#post-2477939</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-159209/scp-543#post-2477939</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 23 Mar 2016 13:13:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dr Nikolaus</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1691109</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is a really interesting article. That is, with the clinical tone presented. For example:</p> <blockquote> <p>She stressed the size of the space - &quot;bigger than anything you've seen,&quot; &quot;bigger than anything ever&quot;. Beginning of claustrophobic tendencies.</p> </blockquote> <p>and</p> <blockquote> <p>Once again she emphasized their size, becoming agitated when interviewers &quot;did not get it&quot;. Severe claustrophobia, anxiety, night terrors.</p> </blockquote> <p>It's not a big deal, and it doesn't affect my opinion on the article, but it is interesting nonetheless.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
